<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>
  <!--
    Save Our Ship 2 / Universum parity for the Shipcracker set.

    VFEP's own 1.6/Patches/SOS2Patch.xml makes its warcasket armor and helmets
    space-worthy when either mod is active: it adds
    the EVA apparel tag and overrides Insulation_Cold to a flat 100. It matches
    its defs by an explicit defName list, not by parent or tag, so a third-party
    warcasket parented on the same VFEP bases gets nothing. This file does the
    same two operations to SCWC_Warcasket_Shipcracker and
    SCWC_WarcasketHelmet_Shipcracker. Shoulder pads are left alone, as in VFEP.

    Gate: PatchOperationFindMod on the display names "Save Our Ship 2" and
    "Universum", copied verbatim from VFEP's patch ON PURPOSE. CLAUDE.md's rule
    to gate on package ids (LoadFolders IfModActive) is for this mod's own
    optional content; here the point is to fire under exactly the same
    condition as VFEP's patch, so a VFEP set and the Shipcracker can never
    disagree about whether warcaskets are EVA-rated. If VFEP ever changes its
    gate, change this one to match.

    Both xpaths match on the values these defs declare directly (apparel/tags
    is a list node, statBases/Insulation_Cold a leaf), so the operations are
    independent of VFEP's abstract bases. PatchOperationReplace on a leaf needs
    the value to carry the element name, hence <Insulation_Cold> inside <value>.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Save Our Ship 2</li>
      <li>Universum</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>
        <li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
          <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName = "SCWC_Warcasket_Shipcracker" or defName = "SCWC_WarcasketHelmet_Shipcracker"]/apparel/tags</xpath>
          <value>
            <li>EVA</li>
          </value>
        </li>
        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/VFEPirates.WarcasketDef[defName = "SCWC_Warcasket_Shipcracker" or defName = "SCWC_WarcasketHelmet_Shipcracker"]/statBases/Insulation_Cold</xpath>
          <value>
            <Insulation_Cold>100</Insulation_Cold>
          </value>
        </li>
      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>
</Patch>
